  "findings": [
    {
      "detail": "The first v4 build (not committed) wrote scale-relief STLs that FAILED the validator: 3 triangles each under the 1e-10 mm2 degenerate cut (edges ~1e-5 mm, left by the 1e-5 mm grid snap), and the build did not gate relief validity. Fixes: the relief file is now gated on the validator, and every v4 export is simplified at 1e-4 mm after the snap and snapped again (volume change recorded per file). The v3 relief files were not re-exported; their smallest triangle is 1.07e-10 mm2, just above the cut.",
      "id": "relief_degenerate_triangles_before_cleanup",
      "status": "fixed in these bytes, kept on record"
    },
    {
      "detail": "fish3d-v3c-daane-length-prop-glide-pose (v3b's assumed glide pose on v3c, membrane 1.2 x wall) was built and FAILED the 12,000-sample wall gate: minimum 0.975 mm against the 1.0 mm rule on its cambered fins (its 3,000-sample minimum was 1.066 mm, a pass). The camber is a vertical offset, so a membrane of thickness t measures t cos(slope) across its surface. It is not published. A thicker membrane (1.5 x wall) is proposed in V4_PENDING and will be built and checked as an additive revision. The frozen v3b prop uses the same camber with a 1.2 x membrane; its own 3,000-sample minimum is 1.079 mm.",
      "id": "glide_pose_prop_failed_dense_wall",
      "status": "withheld from this set; unresolved"
    }
  ],
